sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Payment dispute and chargeback management
    accDescr: Illustrative payment-dispute sequence showing intake, eligibility and time-limit decisions, evidence rework, temporary-credit controls, chargeback response, escalation, and final outcomes.

    autonumber
    participant Customer
    participant Case as Dispute Case Service
    participant Operations as Account Operations
    participant Network as Merchant or Network
    participant Escalation as Escalation Body

    Customer->>Case: Submit payment dispute and available evidence
    Case->>Case: Register case and check applicable time limit
    alt Time limit exceeded
        Case-->>Customer: Explain time-limit outcome and retain case record
        Note over Case,Customer: Terminal outcome: close out-of-time dispute
    else Within applicable time limit
        Case->>Operations: Review transaction, reason, and initial evidence
        alt Resolved directly with merchant or customer
            Operations-->>Case: Confirm refund, cancellation, or explanation
            Case-->>Customer: Communicate agreed outcome
            Note over Case,Customer: Terminal outcome: close as directly resolved
        else Further assessment is required
            alt Evidence is incomplete
                Case->>Customer: Request missing documents or clarification
                alt Evidence received by deadline
                    Customer-->>Case: Supply requested information
                else Evidence not received by deadline
                    Case-->>Customer: Explain insufficient-evidence outcome
                    Note over Case,Customer: Terminal outcome: close dispute
                end
            else Evidence is complete
                Case->>Case: Record evidence readiness
            end

            Case->>Operations: Validate claim under applicable rules
            alt Claim is ineligible
                Operations-->>Case: Record ineligible-claim rationale
                Case-->>Customer: Explain outcome and next steps
                Note over Case,Customer: Terminal outcome: close dispute
            else Claim is eligible
                Operations->>Operations: Assess temporary credit or account hold
                opt Temporary protection is approved
                    Operations-->>Customer: Apply temporary credit or account hold
                end
                Operations->>Network: Submit chargeback or dispute package
                alt No response by the applicable deadline
                    Network-->>Operations: Apply default outcome
                    Operations->>Case: Record final adjustment
                else Response received
                    Network-->>Operations: Send response and supporting evidence
                    Operations->>Operations: Assess customer claim and response
                    alt Customer claim is supported
                        Operations->>Case: Uphold claim and arrange final adjustment
                    else Customer claim is not supported
                        alt Further escalation is permitted
                            Operations->>Escalation: Submit controlled escalation or arbitration case
                            Escalation-->>Operations: Return decision
                        else Escalation is not permitted
                            Operations->>Case: Decline claim and reverse temporary credit if appropriate
                        end
                    end
                end
                Case-->>Customer: Communicate final outcome
                Note over Case,Customer: Terminal outcome: close with documented decision
            end
        end
    end
